; FALLFEST.SCR — Fayd Fall Festival (reusable, "Fayd-annual" seasonal event)
; =============================================================================
; NOT part of LEGENDS.CFG. Upload it in the GM panel (GM Scripts) as a draft,
; Activate it for the festival days, and Disable it afterwards (disabling takes
; it back out of the running game) — see original/HALLOWEEN_RUNBOOK.md.
;
; REQUIRES FESTITEMS.SCR (permanent, in LEGENDS.CFG): vocabulary and the
; festival goods sold here (INUMBER 9350-9357) are defined there so purchases
; outlive this file.
;
; Load order: FALLFEST.SCR first, then (optionally) a year's story file such as
; HALLOWEEN2026.SCR. The story file redefines room 287 and must load AFTER this
; one (give it a lower Admin-panel priority, or simply upload it second).
;
; What this file does:
;   * Festival goods in existing, non-seasonal Fayd shops:
;       199  Randolphs            spider rings, spiderweb earcuffs
;       359  Tailor's Shop        festival shirts, festival masks
;       398  Aunt Emma's Bakery   sugar skulls, caramel apples, pumpkin pie,
;                                 pumpkin bread, spiced cider
;   * Room 287 (Poor Quarter, outside the cemetery gate) becomes the festival
;     lot: campfire, free refreshments, a balloon cart, a fortune-telling
;     crystal ball. Treasure balloons pop open with a prize.
;   * Nine Halloween monsters (MNUMBER 9350-9358) for GMs to @genmon, plus an
;     opt-in cemetery spawner.
;   * Ambient CEVENT echoes (revelers in the streets, chill winds at the gate).
;
; GM switches (named variables, all 0 when the file is first loaded):
;   @set HWQUIET 1    silence the festival/cemetery ambience (0 = on, default)
;   @set HWHAUNT 1    let Halloween monsters spawn in the cemetery (default off)
;
; ID ranges reserved for this file (the 93xx block is Halloween/Fall Festival;
; HALLOWEEN2026.SCR uses 9300-9349, this file 9350-9399):
;   NOUNDEF 9350-9351 + ADJDEF 9350-9356 + INUMBER 9350-9357 (in FESTITEMS.SCR)
;   MADJDEF 9350-9357   INUMBER 9360-9365 (+739 override)   MNUMBER 9350-9358
;   MACRO 9350-9353     CEVENT 9350-9352
;
; Note: the user's original balloon draft used ADJDEF 9108/9109 for
; "treasure"/"spiderweb". Those are 9350/9351 (in FESTITEMS.SCR) because 91xx is the
; ITEMSNEW.SCR armor/shield crafting range and will keep growing.
; =============================================================================

; ── Vocabulary ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
; Nouns/adjectives and the festival goods (INUMBER 9350-9357) live in the
; permanent FESTITEMS.SCR, so purchases survive after this file is removed.

MADJDEF	9350	cackling
MADJDEF	9351	wailing
MADJDEF	9352	stitched
MADJDEF	9353	gill
MADJDEF	9354	headless
MADJDEF	9355	grinning
MADJDEF	9356	pale
MADJDEF	9357	shrieking

VARIABLE HWQUIET
VARIABLE HWHAUNT
VARIABLE HWRND
VARIABLE HWRND2

; ── Macros ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
; Each body is wrapped in an always-true IFVAR so every action parses as part of
; a nested block (bare top-level macro lines only accept a whitelist of actions).

; MACRO 9350: pop a balloon (shared by POKE/POP/RIP). A balloon is a treasure
; balloon if it was bought as one (store adjective 9350 "treasure", which BUY
; puts in ADJ3) or a GM made it one with VAL5 > 0.
MACRO 9350
IFVAR DUMMY9 = 0
  EQUAL DUMMY4 0
  IFVAR ITEMVAL5 > 0
    EQUAL DUMMY4 1
  ENDIF
  IFVAR ITEMADJ3 = 9350
    EQUAL DUMMY4 1
  ENDIF
  IFVAR DUMMY4 = 1
    RANDOM DUMMY5 1 15
    IFVAR DUMMY5 <= 5
      ECHO PLAYER The balloon goes 'pop'! THIS IS A TREASURE BALLOON! You won a black plastic spider ring!
      ECHO OTHERS %N's balloon goes 'pop' and a plastic spider ring falls into %h hands.
      NEWITEM -1 9355 ADJ1=25 ADJ2=587
    ENDIF
    IFVAR DUMMY5 > 5
      IFVAR DUMMY5 <= 10
        ECHO PLAYER The balloon goes 'pop'! THIS IS A TREASURE BALLOON! You won a glowing enamelled skull pin!
        ECHO OTHERS %N's balloon goes 'pop' and a glowing enamelled skull pin drops into %h hands.
        NEWITEM -1 318 ADJ1=145 ADJ2=448 ADJ3=714
      ENDIF
    ENDIF
    IFVAR DUMMY5 > 10
      ECHO PLAYER The balloon goes 'pop'! THIS IS A TREASURE BALLOON! You won a silver spiderweb earcuff!
      ECHO OTHERS %N's balloon goes 'pop' and a silver spiderweb earcuff drops into %h hands.
      NEWITEM -1 9356 ADJ1=292
    ENDIF
    REMOVEITEM -1
  ELSE
    ECHO PLAYER The balloon goes 'pop'! There was no treasure.
    ECHO OTHERS %N's balloon goes 'pop'!
    REMOVEITEM -1
  ENDIF
ENDIF

; MACRO 9351: help yourself to pumpkin bread from the festival table.
MACRO 9351
IFVAR DUMMY9 = 0
  EQUAL DUMMY1 0
  IFCARRY 9354
    EQUAL DUMMY1 1
  ENDIF
  IFVAR DUMMY1 = 1
    ECHO PLAYER You already have some pumpkin bread. Leave a slice for the others!
  ELSE
    ECHO PLAYER You help yourself to a thick slice of warm pumpkin bread.
    ECHO OTHERS %N takes a slice of pumpkin bread from the table.
    NEWITEM -1 9354
  ENDIF
ENDIF

; MACRO 9352: ladle yourself some hot spiced cider from the festival table.
MACRO 9352
IFVAR DUMMY9 = 0
  EQUAL DUMMY1 0
  IFCARRY 9353
    EQUAL DUMMY1 1
  ENDIF
  IFVAR DUMMY1 = 1
    ECHO PLAYER You already have some spiced cider. Drink up before you take more!
  ELSE
    ECHO PLAYER You ladle out a steaming portion of spiced cider. It smells of cinnamon, clove and apples.
    ECHO OTHERS %N ladles out a steaming portion of spiced cider.
    NEWITEM -1 9353
  ENDIF
ENDIF

; MACRO 9353: the crystal ball's fortunes.
MACRO 9353
IFVAR DUMMY9 = 0
  ECHO PLAYER You lay your hands upon the crystal ball. Mist swirls within it, coils, and forms words only you can read:
  ECHO OTHERS %N lays %h hands upon the crystal ball. Mist swirls within it.
  EQUAL ROUNDTIME 5
  RANDOM DUMMY1 1 16
  IFVAR DUMMY1 = 1
    ECHO PLAYER "A light will be lit for you by one who is not living."
    GMMSG %N's fortune: "A light will be lit for you by one who is not living."
  ENDIF
  IFVAR DUMMY1 = 2
    ECHO PLAYER "What is buried is not always lost. What is lost is not always buried."
    GMMSG %N's fortune: "What is buried is not always lost. What is lost is not always buried."
  ENDIF
  IFVAR DUMMY1 = 3
    ECHO PLAYER "Beware the stranger who offers you candy... unless it is very good candy."
    GMMSG %N's fortune: "Beware the stranger who offers you candy... unless it is very good candy."
  ENDIF
  IFVAR DUMMY1 = 4
    ECHO PLAYER "Your shadow knows a secret. Do not turn around too quickly."
    GMMSG %N's fortune: "Your shadow knows a secret. Do not turn around too quickly."
  ENDIF
  IFVAR DUMMY1 = 5
    ECHO PLAYER "An old debt will be paid tonight, though not by you."
    GMMSG %N's fortune: "An old debt will be paid tonight, though not by you."
  ENDIF
  IFVAR DUMMY1 = 6
    ECHO PLAYER "The dead remember every name. Speak yours kindly."
    GMMSG %N's fortune: "The dead remember every name. Speak yours kindly."
  ENDIF
  IFVAR DUMMY1 = 7
    ECHO PLAYER "Something with too many legs admires your hat."
    GMMSG %N's fortune: "Something with too many legs admires your hat."
  ENDIF
  IFVAR DUMMY1 = 8
    ECHO PLAYER "Follow the light, but count your steps."
    GMMSG %N's fortune: "Follow the light, but count your steps."
  ENDIF
  IFVAR DUMMY1 = 9
    ECHO PLAYER "Great fortune lies beneath your feet. So does a great deal of mud."
    GMMSG %N's fortune: "Great fortune lies beneath your feet. So does a great deal of mud."
  ENDIF
  IFVAR DUMMY1 = 10
    ECHO PLAYER "A cold hand will grasp yours before the night is out. Try not to scream."
    GMMSG %N's fortune: "A cold hand will grasp yours before the night is out. Try not to scream."
  ENDIF
  IFVAR DUMMY1 = 11
    ECHO PLAYER "The pumpkin bread is safe. The cider... is also safe. Probably."
    GMMSG %N's fortune: "The pumpkin bread is safe. The cider... is also safe. Probably."
  ENDIF
  IFVAR DUMMY1 = 12
    ECHO PLAYER "Every stone in Fayd was laid over someone else's story."
    GMMSG %N's fortune: "Every stone in Fayd was laid over someone else's story."
  ENDIF
  IFVAR DUMMY1 = 13
    ECHO PLAYER "You will be offered a choice between gold and honor. Take the honor. Then ask about the gold."
    GMMSG %N's fortune: "You will be offered a choice between gold and honor. Take the honor. Then ask about the gold."
  ENDIF
  IFVAR DUMMY1 = 14
    ECHO PLAYER "A balloon will bring you joy. Another will bring you a spider."
    GMMSG %N's fortune: "A balloon will bring you joy. Another will bring you a spider."
  ENDIF
  IFVAR DUMMY1 = 15
    ECHO PLAYER "The gate is chained to keep something in. Not everything respects chains."
    GMMSG %N's fortune: "The gate is chained to keep something in. Not everything respects chains."
  ENDIF
  IFVAR DUMMY1 = 16
    ECHO PLAYER The mist simply forms a small, smug face, sticks out its tongue, and fades away.
    GMMSG %N's fortune: (the crystal ball stuck its tongue out)
  ENDIF
ENDIF

; Balloon (ITEM1.SCR #739, overridden for the festival). Original RIP-only
