;
; Restless spirit — reserved for story files (HALLOWEEN2026.SCR uses its own
; MNUMBER 9300); 9359 left free.

; ── Rooms ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

; 287 — the festival lot outside the Old Fayd Cemetery gate. Base: FAYD.SCR /
; FAYD<season>.SCR room 287 (gate portal, thieves' alley, exits unchanged).
; MONSTER_GROUP 2 removed so Poor Quarter toughs don't spawn into the party.
NUMBER 287
NAME Poor Quarter, festival lot
OUTDOOR_OTHER
FIXED_LIGHT
CALL 33
*DESCRIPTION_START
Rubble has been cleared from the west end of this alley to make room for the Fall Festival. Strings of paper lanterns sway between the leaning tenements, and logs have been dragged into a ring around a crackling campfire to serve as benches. A trestle table sags beneath pumpkin bread and a steaming kettle of hot cider, free to all, and a gaudy striped balloon cart is parked against one wall beside a velvet-draped stool where a crystal ball glimmers. Beyond the merriment, an imposing iron gate still seals off the Old Fayd Cemetery, its chains rattling softly whenever the wind finds them.
*DESCRIPTION_END
ITEM 0 219 VAL2=299
ITEM 1 692 val2=644 VAL5=1
ITEM 2 9360
ITEM 3 9361
ITEM 4 9362
ITEM 5 9363
ITEM 6 9364
ITEM 7 9365
ITEM 9 693 ADJ1=10
EXIT E 286
EXIT ABOVE 2152
*DESCRIPTION_START ITEM EXAM 2
A cheerful fire of split logs crackles inside a ring of old grave-curbing stones. Sparks drift up into the dark and wink out among the paper lanterns.
*DESCRIPTION_END
*DESCRIPTION_START ITEM EXAM 3
A long trestle table covered in an orange cloth. A hand-lettered card propped against the kettle reads, "Help yourself! -- the Festival Committee." (GET BREAD or GET CIDER)
*DESCRIPTION_END
*DESCRIPTION_START ITEM EXAM 6
A wooden cart painted in loud stripes of orange and black, with dozens of balloons bobbing on strings tied to its rail. A price board is nailed to the side.
*DESCRIPTION_END
*DESCRIPTION_START ITEM READ 6
         ~ BALLOONS ~
  Orange, black, purple or white ..... 1 shilling
  TREASURE balloon ................... 1 crown
